---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="While We're Here Privacy Policy"
      description="Privacy Policy for While We're Here, an offline-first conversation card game for iOS."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <article class="policy tile">
        <p class="tile-kicker">While We're Here</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="date"><strong>Effective:</strong> September 9, 2026</p>

        <p>
          While We're Here is a conversation card game for iOS. There is no account to create,
          no login, and no server run by this app. This policy explains what stays on your
          device and what happens when you buy or restore the one-time unlock.
        </p>

        <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>
          The questions you write, your named decks, your favorites, which cards you have
          played or skipped, and where you stopped in a session are stored in the app's local
          storage on your device. The app also stores whether you have seen the introduction
          and whether the lifetime unlock is active, so that play keeps working offline.
        </p>
        <p>
          This app does not upload your questions or your play history, and it does not use
          iCloud sync for them. It does not collect gameplay analytics.
        </p>

        <h2>Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          The full library is a single one-time purchase. Apple processes the purchase itself;
          this app never receives your payment card details.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app uses RevenueCat as its purchase layer. RevenueCat processes purchase history
          and an anonymous identifier that it assigns to your installation, so the app can
          confirm whether the unlock is active, restore a previous purchase, and provide
          purchase analytics to the developer. The app does not send RevenueCat a name, email
          address, custom user ID, advertising identifier, or any of your card text. Apple and
          RevenueCat handle the information they receive under their own policies:
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Apple's Privacy Policy</a
          >
          and
          <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >RevenueCat's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>When the app uses the network</h2>
        <p>
          Buying the unlock, restoring purchases, and refreshing your purchase status require an
          internet connection. Playing does not: once access is established on your device, the
          cards work offline.
        </p>

        <h2>Sharing cards</h2>
        <p>
          You can choose to export your cards to a file. That is always something you start, and
          you choose where the file goes. An exported file contains your questions, follow-ups,
          and deck names. It does not contain your play history or favorites, and it is not a
          full backup. Once you send or save that file somewhere, the service or device you
          chose handles it under its own terms.
        </p>

        <h2>What the app does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No advertising, ad networks, or advertising identifier.</li>
          <li>No app-owned account, login, or cloud sync of your writing.</li>
          <li>No tracking across other apps and websites, and no App Tracking Transparency prompt.</li>
          <li>No crash-reporting or analytics SDK for gameplay.</li>
          <li>No access to contacts, location, microphone, camera, or notifications.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Keeping and deleting your information</h2>
        <p>
          Deleting the app removes its local storage, including your written cards, decks,
          favorites, and history, from that device. Restoring a purchase restores access to the
          full library; it does not bring back cards you deleted or data removed with the app.
          Purchase records held by Apple and RevenueCat are kept under their own retention
          practices and are not deleted by removing the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have a question about purchase information associated with your installation,
          email the address below and describe the issue. Because the app assigns no identity
          to you, some requests may need information from your Apple purchase receipt to act on.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The questions are written for a general audience and are intended to be used together,
          out loud. The app does not knowingly collect personal information from anyone,
          including children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If the app adds a feature that changes what is processed — for example an account,
          sync, or analytics — this policy will be updated before that feature ships, and the
          effective date above will change.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .date {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
